# BUILT.LOG

Delivered intent record. Append-only; corrections preserve history.

Entry format (2026-11-16 onward): one JSON record per build —
  { record_type: "built", build_id: "BLD-####" (sequential),
    created_at: actual clock ISO-8601, title,
    expected: {file_count, folder_count},
    output: {files[], folders[]},
    validation: {status, expected_file_count, actual_file_count,
                 missing_files[], unexpected_files[], evidence[]} }
Declare expected counts, list exact output paths, then validate them against
the filesystem — never assume. Actions without file outputs (merges, prunes,
repairs) belong in validation.evidence. Earlier entries are preserved prose
history.

## 2026-11-12 — Role-fit restructure (user-directed layout)

User intent delivered: "the clean repo no longer has contract and system host;
find and fit contract/runtime material per skill/<role>; each role gets
output/ for artifacts."

- Implementation: 96-file `git mv` redistribution (blob multiset verified
  identical pre/post), import-statement rewrite (130 files / 384 lines),
  path-string and workflow/doc/config updates, boundary tests re-pinned to the
  new layout, retired-path policy extended to `contracts/` and `system/`.
- Evidence: compileall exit 0; import smoke test OK; full pytest run with zero
  failures (see CHANGE.LOG 2026-11-12 for caveats); `ruff check .` clean.
- Unfinished/known: `ruff format --check` failures pre-date this change;
  GitHub push of branch `consolidation-v2` still pending user's interactive
  GitHub authentication.

## 2026-11-11 — Package 1 baseline + structure corrections + mvp-consumer migration (A0)

Requirement IDs / intent:
- Package 1 (baseline) deliverables; user-directed structure decisions
  (roles own runtime+contract, dispatch dissolved into runtime, system/
  retained as slim infra layer, capabilities pending approval).

Actually implemented:
- `agent/skills/{coder,planner,builder,researcher}/__main__.py`: thin role
  entries (coder = read-only capability CLI; researcher/planner/builder =
  fail-closed dispatch reporters). Verified by execution.
- `system/host/file_operations.py`: `write_atomic` byte-exactness fix
  (`newline=""`) — build effects no longer translate newlines on Windows.
- `agent/skills/planner/review/gap_analysis.py`: `_resolve_revision` rejects
  option-like git revisions (argument-injection hardening).
- A0 mvp-consumer migration: `test_host_dispatch.py` repointed to
  HostController-native harness; `test_host_integrity.py` reduced to its four
  pure-host receipt/transition tests; `test_scanner_entrypoints.py` created
  (repointed CLI scanner test); seven MVP-product test/fixture files removed
  (test_mvp_api, test_mvp_service, test_mvp_connectors, test_mvp_mcp_research,
  test_mvp_scanner, test_audit_integration, fixtures/mcp_research_server).
- Guidance: `AGENTS.md` full rewrite (structure, Meta host section, plan-first
  role rule, stdlib rules); `D:\breakdown-v1\DECOMPOSITION_PLAN.md` maintained
  (dispatch dissolution, SDK findings, stdlib folds, system/ restructure).

Evidence:
- pytest collection rc=0 (0 errors); focused tests rc=0 (16/16 pass, with
  --basetemp workaround for a pre-existing Windows temp-dir permission issue);
  guard rc=0 (286 tracked paths accepted); auditor rescan owned findings 0
  (was 71: 60 mvp-import, 9 command-execution review, 2 comment false
  positives). Full-suite result recorded in D:\breakdown-v1\full_suite.txt.

Not done / differs from intent:
- Research-execution recovery semantics (S5) previously covered by
  mvp.research_host are not yet re-implemented in the supported tree — they
  are recorded in the Five Contract Scenarios doc as Package 5/9 requirements.
- Plans (decomposition phases B1/B2/C, capabilities) remain proposals pending
  approval; no dissolution code executed yet.
- 2026-11-14 — system/scanner engine (commit 0ba13c9): rebuilt as fresh
  implementation per approved scanner plan v2. Paths: system/scanner/
  {__init__,__main__,_types,_index,_debug,_preflight,_predict}.py,
  system/__init__.py, tests/system/scanner/{test_index,test_cli}.py
  (16 tests). Evidence: scanner tests 16/16, full suite all-pass,
  ruff check+format clean, guard accepts 216 tracked paths, mypy clean
  except two known errors in orphaned verify_all.py and
  contracts/workflow/validation/planning.py (import the deleted scanner
  contract; disposition frozen under the hard boundary). Also in this
  commit: MEM.LOG hard-boundary record, planner __main__/planning.py
  gap fixes from 5bd9c72. Unfinished: guard-list ruling, evidence-
  separation review, wheel/deptry pass — all pending user instruction.
- 2026-11-14 — role-validator relocation (commit 350872a): planning,
  research and audit-discovery validators moved out of
  shared/contracts/workflow/validation/ into their owning roles
  (planner/contracts/validation.py, researcher/contracts/validation.py,
  auditor/contracts/validation.py); shared __init__ rewritten to
  cross-role only; scanner-coupled traced detector not moved (retired
  stack); benchmark_decision_trace.py and evaluate_gap_sklearn.py
  deleted. Evidence: full suite all-pass, ruff clean, guard 226 paths,
  mypy reduced to the single frozen verify_all.py orphan. Untouched:
  host_gap_analyzer.py (frozen evidence-review candidate),
  shared/host/, shared/storage/, queue location ruling (pending).
- 2026-11-14 — Queue storage relocation: system/storage/ now owns the
  queue (TaskTodo, ExecTodo, Event models + file-backed append-only
  Storage + sys_ref). Old homes deleted: agents/shared/queue,
  agents/shared/events, agents/system/_storage.py, agents/system/_ref.py.
  Guard: system/storage/ ban removed by user ruling. Evidence: full
  suite all-pass, ruff check+format clean, guard accepts 224 tracked
  paths, mypy reduced to the single frozen verify_all.py orphan.
- 2026-11-14 — CI rewrite (this commit): all 10 legacy workflows deleted
  (referenced retired agent/ paths, deleted benchmarks, dead branches,
  Modal/MVP demos); one new .github/workflows/ci.yml with two jobs:
